name=Wandering Hordes Performance Fix [B42]
id=WanderingHordesPerformanceFix
author=druid
description=Add-on for Wandering Hordes: fixes what it costs in performance, without changing it. 1) Multiplayer clients: B42 runs Wandering Hordes' server code on every client too, where nothing uses its results (its wall scanners every frame, its migration map at game start with a half-second freeze and again every game day, its horde managers, a call on every zombie update); the add-on lets only the server run it. 2) Saves: Wandering Hordes remembers walls and fences for every tile any player has ever been near and never forgets any (58 MB of a 76 MB global_mod_data.bin on a real co-op save: a freeze at every world save, seconds at every start); the add-on keeps that map only within 400 tiles (setting) of the players, of where they joined, of offline players and of safehouses; far away Wandering Hordes simply scans the area again when someone comes back. Pure Lua; Wandering Hordes itself is not changed. Settings: the host's sandbox options, page Wandering Hordes: Performance Fix (an admin can change them in a running game). Formerly Wandering Hordes Save Trim. Single player and multiplayer (server and every player).
require=\WanderingHordesCore
category=mechanic
versionMin=42.21
modversion=2.0.0
poster=poster.png
icon=icon.png
